From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH wsi 018] panvk: trim the Android WSI present path

Present called DeviceWaitIdle() on every frame, asked the mapper for the AHB
geometry with AHardwareBuffer_describe() on every frame, and copied the frame
row by row even when the window buffer and the AHB had the same stride.

- Drop DeviceWaitIdle() when wsi->sw: wsi_common_queue_present() waits on
  swapchain->fences[image_index] before calling queue_present(). That fence is
  signaled by the per-image submit once the app's rendering submit completed,
  so the GPU is done with the AHB. The dma-buf path and any
  sw_fence_wait_in_present_thread user keep the full device flush.
- Cache width/height/stride at swapchain creation; no mapper query per present.
- Use one memcpy() for the frame when the strides match and the full width is
  visible, keep the row loop otherwise.
- Pass the damaged region to ANativeWindow_lock() as inOutDirtyBounds so the
  compositor only recomposites what the app reported. The frame is still
  copied in full: a partial copy is unsafe because ANativeWindow gives the
  producer no buffer-age query.

Purpose: cut per-frame overhead on the linear-copy present path.
Tested GPU: build only (aarch64-linux-android29-clang), not yet run on device.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: wsi/016, wsi/017.
Validation test: TBD, on-device present smoke test.

